            <ArticleTitle>Sleep Is for Forgetting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>464-473</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1523/JNEUROSCI.0820-16.2017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is possible that one of the essential functions of sleep is to take out the garbage, as it were, erasing and &quot;forgetting&quot; information built up throughout the day that would clutter the synaptic network that defines us. It may also be that this cleanup function of sleep is a general principle of neuroscience, applicable to every creature with a nervous system.</AbstractText>
